  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Aldehyde, alpha-hydroxy ketone and hemiacetals give positive Tollen&#39;s test. Enol which can get converted into aldehyde through tautomerism are also give positive Tollen&#39;s test.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;is aldehyde,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;get converted into ketones through tautomerism,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;get converted into aldehyde through tautomerism and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;is hemiacetal&nbsp;so,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;will not give positive Tollen&#39;s test.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/25e669b6-090d-4b66-ab3b-86a0ffcf3ead-9ddc9bff-5f44-498b-98a3-99f934936bf7-image.png\" style=\"width: 675px; height: 386px;\" /></p>",
